    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκύλλᾰ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ης</span>, ἡ, <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Ag.</u>
			1233
		</span></i>, 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκύλλη</span></b> , <u>Scylla</u>,
			<i><span class="en">
			Od.
			12.85
		</span></i>, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
			A.
		</span></i> l.c., etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκύλλαν αὐλεῖν</span>,
		in allusion to a composition bearing that name, <i><span class="en">
			Arist.
			<u>Po.</u>
			1461b32
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς λεγομέναις Ἐχίδναις καὶ
					Σκύλλαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Crass.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			 (as 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκυτάλαις</span>
			). (Derivation fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλαξ</span>
			(prob. erroneous) is implied in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.86
			</span></i>.)</div>
